{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-e4aa0217b3a6", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:09.239Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 0, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:17.390Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 13375, "tokens_out": 104, "latency": 8.1248, "finish_reason": "tool_use"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "I'll search the Thornfield Mutual documents for information about the fraud referral procedure.", "response_hash": "sha256:8cab5dbb585e1887bc58597ddcd30f9dcd3890174037413e2ee832c64ada6fb3", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
{"astp_version": "0.1.0", "event_type": "turn", "session": {"id": "s-e4aa0217b3a6", "start_time": "2026-09-22T10:38:09.239Z", "user_id": "u-claims-0417", "tenant_id": "thornfield-mutual", "client_app": "claims-copilot", "agent_id": "astp-lab-agent-1", "config_version": "0.2.0"}, "turn": {"index": 1, "timestamp": "2026-09-22T10:38:17.731Z", "model_id": "claude-haiku-4-5", "model_version": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "tokens_in": 14613, "tokens_out": 370, "latency": 0.3398, "finish_reason": "end_turn"}, "content": {"prompt_text": "What is the fraud referral procedure, and at what point does a claim have to be referred?", "prompt_hash": "sha256:c41eae1b6df85dd983a6d0ffba0a08a6dfe3f2fbe0e42bfdec85cc5c09acf816", "response_text": "Based on the Thornfield Mutual fraud referral procedure (prc-fraud-002):\n\n## When to refer\n\n**Referral is warranted where two or more of the following indicators are present, or where any one of them is strongly present:**\n\n- The policy was taken out or increased within thirty days of the incident\n- The incident happened at an unusual hour with no independent witness\n- Documents supplied are copies where originals would be expected, or carry inconsistent dates, fonts or reference numbers\n- The claimant is unusually familiar with policy wording or claims process\n- The same address, bank account or telephone number appears on unconnected claims\n- Injuries reported do not match the damage to the vehicle or property\n- The claimant presses for a quick cash settlement and declines an inspection\n- Receipts are sequential, from a single supplier, and round numbered\n\n## The procedure\n\n1. **Refer, don't investigate** – raise a referral on the counter fraud queue and carry on handling the claim normally\n2. **Discretion** – do not tell the claimant a referral has been made, and do not mention it in any claimant correspondence\n3. **What to include** – the claim reference, the indicators observed, the documents relied on, and your own note of the conversation (facts only)\n4. **Counter fraud response** – they acknowledge within two working days with one of three outcomes: no further action, monitor, or investigate\n5. **If investigation proceeds** – all claimant contact passes to counter fraud; payments require written agreement from the counter fraud lead\n\nThe key point: you don't decide if fraud has occurred. That decision belongs to the counter fraud team.", "response_hash": "sha256:63fcd6086ddf0668ee910ccb79a0e0c22f582bca956c804e1c30a42ef0138157", "system_prompt_version": "sp-0.2.0", "redaction_applied": false}, "control": {"canary_triggered": false, "policy_version": "0.1.0", "block_reason": null}}
